{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/765392-wraith-mummy-question","id":765392,"title":"Wraith/Mummy question.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-13T23:40:44-08:00","id":765392,"title":"Wraith/Mummy question.","content":"If a human were to have a Ba of 5 and die and return as a Wraith, how would that Ba of 5 translate in Wraith terms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T03:34:26-08:00","id":765453,"title":"","content":"Humans don't have Ba in Wraith. Ba is one of the soul parts that appears by using the rite that creates mummies on a person. Mummy the Resurrection and Wraith do not have the same rules for making &quot;The Dead&quot;, so I don't even get the point of your question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T12:31:47-08:00","id":765713,"title":"","content":"Ba is probably the psyche. The trait wouldn't directly translate to anything in Wraith, because the strength of a Psyche in Wraith is measured by Willpower. A spectre might use Ba to score their Psyche trait though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T22:38:54-08:00","id":766856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cogliostro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/765392-wraith-mummy-question?p=765453#post765453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Humans don't have Ba in Wraith. Ba is one of the soul parts that appears by using the rite that creates mummies on a person. Mummy the Resurrection and Wraith do not have the same rules for making &quot;The Dead&quot;, so I don't even get the point of your question.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, that soul portion exists whether you are alive or dead. And it's usually ONLY humans who have a Ba, though some werewolves and changelings become Wraiths if they make a deal with a Monitor. Ditto with the Ka. <br /> <br /> The Ka is the spiritual part of the body, it's what necromancers use to create zombies, whether they know it by that name or not. The Khu are the Fetter bonds, the Khaibit is the Shadow, and the Sahu is the Edeilon. All of these things besides the Ka have ratings in Wraith, so part of me suspects that the Ba might be tied in to the passions. I am curious though because there is a spell to boost your Ba rating and I am thinking it might be a way to justify taking your average joe mortal and changing him spiritually to the point he might develop an aptitude for sorcery. Assuming not just everybody can pick up a book and learn it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T00:11:25-08:00","id":766893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/765392-wraith-mummy-question?p=766856#post766856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, that soul portion exists whether you are alive or dead. And it's usually ONLY humans who have a Ba, though some werewolves and changelings become Wraiths if they make a deal with a Monitor. Ditto with the Ka.<br /> <br /> The Ka is the spiritual part of the body, it's what necromancers use to create zombies, whether they know it by that name or not. The Khu are the Fetter bonds, the Khaibit is the Shadow, and the Sahu is the Edeilon. All of these things besides the Ka have ratings in Wraith, so part of me suspects that the Ba might be tied in to the passions. I am curious though because there is a spell to boost your Ba rating and I am thinking it might be a way to justify taking your average joe mortal and changing him spiritually to the point he might develop an aptitude for sorcery. Assuming not just everybody can pick up a book and learn it.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you as a storyteller want to include such things in a game for crossovers and the like, go right ahead. That said, Wraith was not written with the intent to recreate the pseudo-Egyptian paradigm from Mummy.<br /> <br /> There are parallels regarding how the games handle the natures of the soul, but that likely has more to do with parallels already existing within death and ghost mythology. I don't think there was any real intent for the concepts of Mummy to represent or interfere with Wraith.<br /> <br /> It is sort of similar to Gnosis/Quit with Werewolf and Mage. The two power sources have things in common but are not the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T02:53:30-08:00","id":766955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/765392-wraith-mummy-question?p=766893#post766893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you as a storyteller want to include such things in a game for crossovers and the like, go right ahead. That said, Wraith was not written with the intent to recreate the pseudo-Egyptian paradigm from Mummy.<br /> <br /> There are parallels regarding how the games handle the natures of the soul, but that likely has more to do with parallels already existing within death and ghost mythology. I don't think there was any real intent for the concepts of Mummy to represent or interfere with Wraith.<br /> <br /> It is sort of similar to Gnosis/Quit with Werewolf and Mage. The two power sources have things in common but are not the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except, in the first two editions of Mummy at least, the Undying spend rather a lot of time in the Underworld between stints in the Skinlands. So they should have some kind of alignment, even if (as always) WW doesn't appear to have made it easy to run crossovers.<br /> <br /> The Wiki states that the Ba is akin to a wraith, and is the part that travels back to the Underworld: <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Soul_(MTR\" target=\"_blank\">http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Soul_(MTR</a>). I'm not sure how much of that article is fan speculation over canon, but it jives with what I thought was the case.<br /> <br /> The Ba rating, however, doesn't seem to replace Willpower, so perhaps it is, as Mercurial suggests, a measure of the strengths of one's Passions (or, at least, their highest rated Passion), since Passions provide the emotional 'strength' for the Psyche to resist Oblivion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 11-17-2015, 05:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T06:52:15-08:00","id":767034,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">We had a conversation along these lines on the forum before where we were trying to find parallels in all dead things (Wraith, Mummy, Vampires, Kuei-jin), I just can't seem to find it.<br /> <br /> If I remember correctly it went like this; </span></span><ul><li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><i>Ka</i> \u2013 This is the part of the soul that protects the Khat (body). Ka = Fetters</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><i>Ba</i> \u2013 This grants strength of character and free thinking. Allows individuality. Ba = Willpower.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><i>Khu</i> \u2013 This part of the soul drives creativity and inspiration. Khu = Pathos/Passions.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><i>Khaibit</i> \u2013 This generates the drive, ambition and aggression. Khaibit = Shadow.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><i>Sahu</i> \u2013 This is the part of the soul that drives the morality of the person. Sahu = Edeilon.</span></span></li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}